----------
> Does anyone have any .OPL snippets they wouild care to share 
> concerning how to call the UNZIP.IMG file via opl, with paths to 
> the files you wish to unzip?

Along the following lines:

proc launch%:(app$,arg$)
local name$(128)
local cmdl$(128)
local pid%, ret%

name$=app$+chr$(0)
cmdl$=arg$+chr$(0)
ret%=call($0187,UADD(addr(name$),1),UADD(addr(cmdl$),1),0,0,addr(pid
%))
if ret%<0
  alert(app$+" process failed",err$(ret%))
  return 0
endif

return pid%
endp

proc resume:(pid%)
call($0688,pid%,0,0,0,0)
endp

Note that unlike the firmware apps, unzip.img is expecting a simple 
zero-terminated command line with space-separated arguments i.e. 
the normal way (none of those mode characters or embedded NULs 
nonsense!).

So the following:

global uzippid%
uzippid%=launch%:("loc::m:\run\unzip.img", "-qq m:\test.zip")
if uzippid%<>0
  resume:(uzippid%)
endif

should extract the archived files *into the current directory* (-qq 
tells it to be very non-verbose).

Not tested, this, BTW.

Regards,

David.
  


